          1,
          182
        ]
      ],
      "review_level": "full_raw_source_body_review",
      "assessment": "Full HTTP boundary read. Narrow loopback peer/host/scheme and same-origin predicates reject duplicate security headers, proxy evidence and ambiguous framing; the docstring correctly separates loopback from authentication. Actual body bytes are capped at limit+1 and duplicate JSON keys/deep recursion become typed refusals before framework parsing. Malformed ordinary JSON is deliberately left to the framework. Supplied ASGI envelope types and a nonnegative integer limit are preconditions rather than checked schemas. Repeated empty more_body messages have no byte-progress or iteration ceiling, so the byte/memory bound is not a total-work or termination guarantee. No receive port was called.",
      "actual_execution_status": "Source review only; no original module, provider, network or native execution. Independent controls, if added, are recorded separately.",
