        ]
      ],
      "review_level": "full_raw_source_body_review",
      "assessment": "Full byte-limit owner read. UTF-8 prefix slicing bounds encoding and hashing by the configured byte ceiling, including a first-decisive overflow versus invalid-surrogate distinction; stream readers stop after observing limit+1 bytes and close supplied iterators. Prefix hashes honestly cover only observed bytes. Endless empty chunks can still consume unbounded iterations, and iterator-close behavior is supplied externally; byte bounds do not prove time/cost/cancellation guarantees. OversizeReceipt checks numeric inequalities and authority label but does not validate exact integer types or digest shape. Direct callers must supply valid limits and stream chunk types. No retained stream/provider code executed.",
