      ],
      "review_level": "full_raw_source_body_review",
      "assessment": "EventStream appends same-aggregate events with strictly increasing versions, allowing gaps unlike AggregateRoot's next-version rule. Constructor accepts a supplied mutable event list without checking its initial contents, and the internal list remains mutable. Error calls pass one argument, which the now-reviewed DomainInvariantError accepts as its code; the error code therefore includes dynamic event text rather than a stable vocabulary. In-memory append-only is a disciplined-use property, not immutable storage.",
