        ]
      ],
      "review_level": "full_raw_source_body_review",
      "assessment": "RepoPath normalizes slashes/dot segments and offers casefolded equal-or-ancestor collision tests. It rejects leading forward slash and unresolved parent escape, but accepts drive-colon paths, NUL, and leading-backslash absolute/UNC spellings after stripping leading slashes. It is not a portable filesystem containment validator. Normalizing a/../b to b also loses the original syntactic distinction; actual symlink containment remains outside scope.",
