      "review_level": "full_raw_source_body_review",
      "assessment": "UtcTimestamp normalizes its internal datetime to aware UTC but preserves raw string spelling, including offset and date-only inputs, in value/to_iso. Naive input is silently interpreted as UTC. Equality compares datetime across subclasses while hash includes concrete type, so a subclass can violate equal-implies-equal-hash. Ordering/expiration are meaningful only under the declared UTC interpretation and supplied reference; now() is ambient clock I/O, not used here.",
