      "assessment": "Chaos helpers are finite scenario checks, not a chaos execution framework. Head-change and PATH_ONLY/NOT_APPLICABLE cases expect specific failures. The strict-measurement helper rejects only NOT_MEASURED, unlike the general STRICT predicate which rejects INJECTED and all other non-MEASURED labels. Self-judge checks use case-sensitive substring membership on unnormalized paths, so case/backslash aliases can evade and incidental substrings can overmatch. No listed protected path or embedded instruction was executed.",
