          1,
          146
        ]
      ],
      "review_level": "full_raw_source_body_review",
      "assessment": "Merge mutex forbids automatic stale takeover and returns an explicit STALE_RECOVERED record before reacquisition; release checks active token ID and expiry. It is mutable in-memory state without thread/process atomicity or durable audit. Recovery does not establish prior worker termination/fencing, and token IDs deterministically repeat for the same holder/time/TTL. NaN time/TTL is not admitted/refused explicitly and can defeat expiry. Comments about serialization need these operational prerequisites.",
      "actual_execution_status": "Source review only; no original module, provider, network or native execution. Independent controls, if added, are recorded separately.",
